GitHub doesn’t provide a “make all repositories private” button directly in the UI, 
but you can absolutely do it quickly using one of these three methods, depending on your comfort level.

  Option 1 — Use GitHub CLI (Fastest & Easiest)

If you’re comfortable with the command line:

 1️Install GitHub CLI

Download from: [https://cli.github.com/](https://cli.github.com/)
Then log in:

gh auth login


 2️Run this one-liner:

This will loop through all your repositories and set their visibility to `private`:


for repo in $(gh repo list YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME --json name --jq '.[].name'); do
  gh repo edit "$repo" --visibility private
  echo "Changed $repo to private"
done


 Notes:

* Replace `YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME` with your actual username.
* You need to be the owner of the repos (not just a collaborator).
* This will skip any repos that are already private.


  Option 2 — Use GitHub REST API (Advanced)

If you prefer using an API or want to automate it in scripts:

 1️Create a Personal Access Token (PAT)

* Go to Settings → Developer Settings → Personal Access Tokens → Tokens (classic)
* Generate a new token with `repo` scope.

 2️Use a `curl` command:


TOKEN=your_personal_access_token
USERNAME=your_github_username

for repo in $(curl -s -H "Authorization: token $TOKEN" "https://api.github.com/user/repos?per_page=100" | jq -r '.[].name'); do
  curl -X PATCH -H "Authorization: token $TOKEN" -H "Accept: application/vnd.github.v3+json" \
    https://api.github.com/repos/$USERNAME/$repo \
    -d '{"private": true}'
  echo "Set $repo to private"
done


🔹 Requires: `jq` installed
🔹 Works for up to 100 repos per page — you can adjust pagination if needed.

---

  Option 3 — Manual (UI)

If you have only a few repos:

1. Go to each repository → Settings
2. Scroll to Danger Zone
3. Click Change repository visibility
4. Choose Private

This is slower but doesn’t need command-line tools.

---

 ⚠️ Important Notes

* Public forks can’t be made private unless you detach them (delete and recreate manually).
* Free accounts can now have unlimited private repos (since 2020), but team members may still count toward billing if using GitHub Pro/Team/Enterprise.
* If you’re part of an organization, ensure you have permission to change visibility.


Ready-to-run PowerShell script for Windows that will change all your public GitHub repositories to private in one click

 PowerShell Script: Make All Your GitHub Repos Private

Copy everything below into a new file, e.g. MakeAllReposPrivate.ps1, and run it from PowerShell after installing Git + GitHub CLI.


# ==============================================
# GitHub Bulk Repository Visibility Changer
# Author: Praveen Madupu (PMSQLDBA)
# Purpose: Change all repositories to PRIVATE mode
# Date: (auto-logged below)
# ==============================================

# ---- Configuration ----
$OrgName = "PMSQLDBA"
$LogFile = "D:\Scripts\GitHub_Private_Change_Log_$(Get-Date -Format 'yyyyMMdd_HHmmss').txt"

# ---- Start Logging ----
Add-Content $LogFile "=== Starting GitHub Repo Visibility Change ==="
Add-Content $LogFile "Date: $(Get-Date)"
Add-Content $LogFile "----------------------------------------------"

# ---- Validate GitHub CLI ----
if (-not (Get-Command gh -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)) {
    Write-Host "GitHub CLI not found. Please install it from https://cli.github.com/" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit
}

# ---- Verify Auth Status ----
$AuthStatus = gh auth status 2>&1
if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) {
    Write-Host "Please authenticate first using: gh auth login --scopes 'repo,admin:repo_hook'" -ForegroundColor Red
    exit
}

# ---- Fetch All Repositories ----
$repos = gh repo list $OrgName --limit 200 --json name,visibility --jq ".[] | [.name, .visibility] | @tsv"

foreach ($line in $repos) {
    $parts = $line -split "`t"
    $repoName = $parts[0]
    $currentVisibility = $parts[1]

    if ($currentVisibility -eq "private") {
        Add-Content $LogFile "$OrgName/$repoName already private"
        continue
    }

    # ---- Attempt to Change Visibility ----
    Write-Host "Changing $repoName to private..." -ForegroundColor Cyan
    gh repo edit "$OrgName/$repoName" --visibility private --accept-visibility-change-consequences 2>&1 | Out-Null

    if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {
        Add-Content $LogFile "$OrgName/$repoName changed to private"
        Write-Host "$repoName → Private" -ForegroundColor Green
    } else {
        Add-Content $LogFile "$OrgName/$repoName failed to change"
        Write-Host "$repoName → Failed" -ForegroundColor Red
    }
}

Add-Content $LogFile "----------------------------------------------"
Add-Content $LogFile "Script completed at $(Get-Date)"
Write-Host "`Completed. Log file saved at: $LogFile" -ForegroundColor Yellow

